  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "Bugfix: spawn._trim_routed_item raises KeyError routed-findings when the packet cap trims a routed-findings item (dispatch failures T-1270, T-1274)",
  "spec": "Root cause found by the Planner: spawn._packet_body builds by_name from the fixed sections list (objective ... evidence) but the active context router also returns a routed-findings section (spawn.py near line 924 appends it separately). When the 4800-char body cap triggers _trim_routed_item(by_name, routed_sections), the loop pops by_name[name] for every name in routed_sections, and routed-findings is not a key of by_name, so KeyError escapes dispatch and the task is marked failed with dispatch error routed-findings. Fix: include routed-findings (and any routed section name) in by_name when the section exists, or make _trim_routed_item skip names absent from by_name while still trimming the routed item; keep the trim order (SHORT, LONG, FULL) and the fence rule. Regression test: a task whose packet exceeds the cap with routed-findings items in active mode builds without raising and the routed-findings section is trimmed last-first like the others. Repository rules: unittest, no new dependencies, run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until green, do not ask questions.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_trim_routed_item_handles_routed_findings_section (packet over the cap with routed-findings items in active mode builds; trimming removes items without KeyError)",
